# Parallel work recognition

Multi-area work fans out to parallel subagents per `.cursor/PARALLEL_WORK.md` (skill `parallel-work`).

When planning such a task:

1. Include a **Parallel workers** section in the plan before presenting it (`PARALLEL_WORK.md` §0):
   - the contract the lead writes first;
   - waves in dependency order, with an agent table per wave (id, model and reason, job, owned files, forbidden files, test commands);
   - the RAM check;
   - the gates and commits;
   - art, sound and creature agents when assets are involved.
2. Use the plan section template in `.cursor/skills/parallel-work/SKILL.md`.
3. When executing, follow the lead checklist in that skill: RAM first, contract first, disjoint ownership, lead-only shared config, gates after each wave.
4. Reuse agents with `SendMessage` before spawning new ones, and `TaskStop` every agent whose work is committed and won't be resumed (`PARALLEL_WORK.md` §5a); finished agents otherwise pile up in Claude Code's agent list.

Skip this for a single-area task or one under ~150 lines; say so in one line in the plan.
